{% set delivered = as_timestamp(states('sensor.audi_widget_bridge_bridge_delivery'), none) %}
{% set age = as_timestamp(now()) - delivered if delivered is not none else none %}
{% if age is none %}
<ha-alert alert-type="warning" title="Audi bridge status unknown">No valid delivery timestamp is available. Check that the bridge is running and connected.</ha-alert>
{% elif age < -300 %}
<ha-alert alert-type="warning" title="Check phone clock">The bridge delivery time is in the future. Check the phone date and time.</ha-alert>
{% elif age > 21600 %}
<ha-alert alert-type="error" title="Audi bridge update overdue">No update delivered for over 6 hours. Last delivery: {{ relative_time(as_datetime(delivered)) }} ago. Open Audi Widget Bridge on the phone and check capture, connection and battery settings.</ha-alert>
{% else %}
<ha-alert alert-type="success" title="Audi bridge receiving updates">Last delivery: {{ relative_time(as_datetime(delivered)) }} ago.</ha-alert>
{% endif %}

This checks delivery to Home Assistant, not whether Audi has fresh data from the car.

{% set received = as_datetime(states('sensor.audi_widget_bridge_widget_received'), none) %}
{% if received %}
{% set age = ((now() - received).total_seconds() / 60) | int %}
**Widget last captured {{ relative_time(received) }} ago.**
{% else %}
**Waiting for a widget reading.**
{% endif %}

Audi's last vehicle contact: **{{ states('sensor.audi_widget_bridge_last_vehicle_contact') }}**.

{% if state_attr('sensor.audi_widget_bridge_widget_data', 'capture_phase') == 'startup_snapshot' %}
The latest reading is a startup snapshot and may contain cached vehicle data.
{% endif %}

Capture and delivery times show when the phone read and sent the widget. They do not establish when the car last reported new data.

## Capture details
- **Capture type:** {{ state_attr('sensor.audi_widget_bridge_widget_data', 'capture_phase') | default('Unknown', true) }}
- **Phone locked at capture:** {{ state_attr('sensor.audi_widget_bridge_widget_data', 'phone_locked') }}
- **Screen interactive at capture:** {{ state_attr('sensor.audi_widget_bridge_widget_data', 'screen_interactive') }}

Vehicle status is displayed as Audi supplies it. No locked/unlocked interpretation is applied.
